// ─── SDK docs — translations for the modern page ──────────────────────────────
// The ten locale blocks inside build-sdk-docs.mjs cover the ORIGINAL page. When
// the page was redesigned (and again when the v1.8 presentation surface landed)
// the new strings were added English-only, with tr() falling back to EN — which
// left nine "localized" pages that were ~90% English.
//
// This module closes that gap: every key added after the original translation
// pass, in all nine non-English languages. Merged over T in build-sdk-docs.mjs.
//
// Conventions:
//   • Identifiers stay in English — method names (add(), whenReady()), option
//     names, event names, types, and product names (three.js, web-ifc,
//     WebAssembly, postMessage, ArrayBuffer, IFC, IDS, EIR, OSM, CORS,
//     Health Score). Translating those would break copy-paste against the API.
//   • Only prose is translated.
//   • Double-quoted strings throughout, so typographic apostrophes need no
//     escaping in fr / it / ca.

